# Personal Expense Tracker

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.12-blue)
![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/Status-Complete-brightgreen)

A simple command-line app to add, view, and delete personal expenses, with data saved locally so it persists between runs.

Built as the capstone project for the **Python Fundamentals** track in [the-rebuild](../../../) — pulls together loops, functions, conditionals, exception handling, and file I/O into one working tool.

---

## What it does

- **Add** an expense with a category, amount, and date
- **View** all expenses recorded so far, with a running total
- **Delete** an expense you no longer want to keep
- **Persist** — expenses save to a local JSON file, so nothing is lost when you close the program

---

## How to run it

```bash
python main.py
```

